Q2. Difference between SRP and ISP

Interview Ready Answer

Single Responsibility Principle (SRP)

• Focuses on Classes.
• A class should have only one responsibility.
• A class should have only one reason to change.
• Solves multiple responsibilities in a class.

------------------------------------------------------------

Interface Segregation Principle (ISP)

• Focuses on Interfaces.
• A class should not implement methods
  it doesn't need.
• Splits large interfaces into
  smaller role-specific interfaces.
• Solves fat interface problems.

------------------------------------------------------------

Example of SRP

class Student{

    void updateDetails(){}

    void calculateGrade(){}
}

These methods belong to

Student Management.

Adding

sendSMS()

would violate SRP.

------------------------------------------------------------

Example of ISP

interface Worker{

    void work();

    void eat();
}

Robot only works.

It does not eat.

Therefore,

forcing Robot to implement eat()

violates ISP.

