Q3. Can implementing multiple interfaces
violate ISP?

Interview Ready Answer

No.

Implementing multiple interfaces does NOT
violate ISP.

In fact,

ISP encourages multiple
small role-specific interfaces.

------------------------------------------------------------

Bad Design

interface Worker{

    void work();

    void eat();

    void drive();
}

Robot implements Worker.

Robot is forced to implement

eat()

drive()

which are unnecessary.

ISP is violated.

------------------------------------------------------------

Good Design

interface Workable{

    void work();
}

interface Eatable{

    void eat();
}

interface Driveable{

    void drive();
}

------------------------------------------------------------

class Human implements Workable,Eatable{

}

class Driver implements Workable,Driveable{

}

class Robot implements Workable{

}

Each class implements only
what it actually needs.

ISP is followed.

